## Key Concepts
- Tombstone semantics, cross-topic propagation, and per-tenant isolation
- Idempotence, retention versus deletion semantics
- Audit trails and verification under failure conditions
- Handling cross-topic joins while preserving deletion markers
- Compression-aware deletion propagation

## Code Example
```javascript
function createTombstone(tenantId, key, deletionTimestamp) {
  return {
    tenantId,
    key,
    deletionTimestamp,
    isTombstone: true
  };
}

function propagateTombstone(tombstone, pipeline) {
  pipeline.forEach(stage => {
    stage.emit(tombstone);
    stage.compress(); // Preserve tombstone through compression
  });
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests memory management in a KCNA sink under idle-key TTL cleanup, ensuring at-least-once processing remains correct after eviction and offsets stay coherent.

## Key Concepts

- Per-key TTL cleanup
- In-memory state with concurrency
- Offset management and idempotence
- Canary-based testing

## Code Example

```javascript
class TTLStateStore {
  constructor(ttlMs) {
    this.ttlMs = ttlMs;
    this.map = new Map();
  }
  processMessage(key, value, t) {
    this.map.set(key, { last: t, value });
  }
  commitOffsets(offsets) {
    // persist offsets
  }
  evictStaleStates(now) {
    for (const [k, v] of this.map.entries()) {
      if (now - v.last > this.ttlMs) this.map.delete(k);
    }
  }
}
```

